# Package .jpl after changes

The user installs this plugin in Joplin from `publish/com.dvreeman.searchsort.jpl`, not only via `dist/`.

After any change that affects the built plugin (source under `src/`, build scripts, webpack config, manifest, etc.):

1. Run `npm run package` (builds and writes the `.jpl`).
2. Confirm `publish/com.dvreeman.searchsort.jpl` has an updated mtime.
3. Tell the user the `.jpl` is ready to reinstall in Joplin.

Do not stop at `npm run build` alone unless the user only asked for a compile check.
